Already working:
- Two Spring services with separate DB schemas.
- Event ingestion → RabbitMQ → signed webhook delivery.
- Outboxes, idempotency, deduplication, retries, DLQ and status updates.
- Registration UI, applications, event types, endpoints, API keys, signing secrets and soft deletion.
- Endpoint timeout, attempt limits and per-instance rate/concurrency limits.

Main remaining work:
- Redis caching, receiver-side rate limits and distributed delivery limits.
- Circuit breakers and manual DLQ replay.
- OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, Grafana, logs and latency metrics.
- gRPC status reconciliation.
- Login, cookies/JWT sessions and RBAC.
- Receiver management and application-level settings.
- App containers, Nginx, cloud deployment and enable/disable policy controls.

The core delivery flow works. Most remaining effort is operational reliability, observability, security and completing the demo experience.

